The '''Shag Pabol'''<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" /> or '''Slave Road''' in [[Galactic Basic Standard|Basic]]<ref name="Scarif">{{EncyclopediaCite|Scarif and Other Planets in the Outer Rim}}</ref> was a [[Hyperspace route|hyperlane]] within [[Hutt Space]]. The [[Delphanian]] [[privateer]] [[Sidon Ithano]] carried a [[letter of marque]] that gave him license to conduct raids along the Shag Pabol, [[Ootmian Pabol]], [[Pabol Hutta]] and all secular hyperlanes in [[Hutt]] Space. The letter also allowed him to deliver any seized cargoes from these raids to his patron Hutt [[kajidic]]s, the [[Desilijic]], [[Ramesh]], [[Besadii]], [[Gnuda]] and [[Shell]].<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Shag Pabol was first mentioned in the new ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] on a supplemental item included in the deluxe edition of the [[2018]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: Smuggler's Guide]]'', which was written by [[Daniel Wallace]].<ref name="Smuggler's Guide" /> The roleplaying game book ''[[Ghosts of Dathomir]]''<ref name="GoD">''[[Ghosts of Dathomir]]''</ref> incorrectly<ref name="GreatKashyyykBranch">{{GalaxyMapHyperlanes|route=Shag Pabol|leg=''[[The Essential Atlas]]''|canon=''[[Star Wars: Smuggler's Guide]]''}}</ref> places [[Toydaria]] on the Shag Pabol<ref name="GoD" /> instead of the [[Oktos Route]], which continues on from the end of the Shag Pabol at the [[Y'Toub system]].

